## 🏗️ Task 1 — Business Flow (In My Own Words)

When someone shows interest in a product, they become a **Lead** in Salesforce.
The sales team contacts them and decides if they are a real prospect.
If yes, the Lead is **converted** — this automatically creates three records:
a **Contact** (the person), an **Account** (their company), and an **Opportunity** (the deal).
The team then works the Opportunity through stages until it is either **won or lost**.

---

## 🏗️ Task 2 — Real-World Mapping: College Admission System

Applying Salesforce objects to a college admission workflow:

| Salesforce Object | College Equivalent |
|------------------|--------------------|
| **Account** | The College / University |
| **Contact** | Admission Counsellor or Faculty |
| **Lead** | Student who submitted an enquiry form |
| **Opportunity** | Student's active admission application |

**Flow:**
```
Student submits enquiry
    → Lead created
    → Counsellor qualifies the student
    → Lead converted:
          Contact  = Student / Guardian
          Account  = The College
          Opportunity = Active Application
    → Application moves through stages:
          Enquired → Documents Submitted → Under Review → Decision
    → Admitted ✅ (Closed Won)  |  Rejected ❌ (Closed Lost)
```

